  "message": "The emulation has no failed checks: the design held together, with every flow connected and no rule violations. It's marked \"blocked\" for a different reason. None of the 8 components has a supported Google Cloud implementation in the generator yet, and the existing repository still needs a plan for how we connect to it without changing it. No change to the diagram will fix this. It's product engineering work: the generator needs native implementations for Cloud Run, Pub/Sub, Secret Manager, Vertex AI and Firestore, plus a read-only repository connection. This run on artifact fb97bef8… is the test case to reproduce the gap, and I won't shrink the design to make the check pass. So we can plan that work, which repository host should we build the read-only connection for first: GitHub, GitLab, Bitbucket or something else?",
